# LRAE exploration_map_merge bootstrap fix (2026-11-03)
#
# Symptom: with Go2 spawning in NewMine, the robot stands up with < 0.1 m of
# horizontal drift.  exploration_map_merge only calls mapMerge() after the
# robot has moved 0.1 m (line "if(abs(ego_position_last.x - ...) >= 0.1 ...)"),
# and the one-shot bootstrap eligibility (ego_position_last initialised to
# mapinitox) is consumed on the first loop iteration, before initSucessed can
# flip.  Result: no global map -> no exploration centroid -> no motion, and
# the merge gate can never be passed.  Whether a run bootstraps depends on the
# robot's random stand-up wobble exceeding 0.1 m.
#
# Fix: run mapMerge() once immediately after initGlobalMap() and publish
# /MoveInited, so the first merged window is available without any motion.
#
# Applies to: ws/src/lrae/lrae_planner/src/exploration_map_merge.cpp
# (LRAE tarball, not a git repo — apply by hand or with patch -p1 from
#  ws/src/lrae).
--- a/lrae_planner/src/exploration_map_merge.cpp
+++ b/lrae_planner/src/exploration_map_merge.cpp
@@ -236,7 +236,14 @@
         if(hasMap && !initSucessed)
         {
             initGlobalMap();
+            // Bootstrap merge: mapMerge() below only runs after the robot has
+            // moved 0.1 m, and ego_position_last was already consumed before
+            // initSucessed could flip.  A robot that stands still at spawn
+            // (Go2 stand-up wobble < 0.1 m) would otherwise deadlock with no
+            // global map, no centroid, and therefore no motion at all.
+            mapMerge();
+            isMoveInited.data = 1;
+            move_inited_pub.publish(isMoveInited);
         }
         geometry_msgs::Pose current_pose_ros;

# ============================================================================
# Fix 2 (same file set, 2026-11-04): narrow-tunnel viewpoint starvation +
# permanent go_home_ latch.
#
# Symptom: in the 10-min NewMine run the robot reached (8.5, 1.1) at ~44 s,
# then the planner reported "The current window has no centroid" every cycle
# and finally "There are almost no explorable unknown regions!" forever; the
# robot pushed into a wall at 0.5 m/s command with ~0 m/s actual speed.
#
# Offline replication of getCentroid/getCentroidHelper on the dumped
# /globalMap at the stall showed: 149 unknown cells adjacent to free space,
# of which 83 are excluded by the 8-neighbour occupied rule, 5 remain with
# exactly 3-4 free neighbours (rule requires exactly 3 or 4), and all 5 are
# excluded by the "no occupied within 2 cells (0.6 m)" visibility rule ->
# viewpoint_fir empty everywhere -> no centroid can be accepted -> fallback
# exhausted -> go_home_count_ > 20 latches go_home_ permanently (upstream
# never clears it).
#
# Fix (exploration_planning.h/.cpp), parameterised, upstream defaults keep
# original behaviour:
#   - vp_free_neighbors_min (default 3): replaces "exactly 3 or 4" with
#     "count_thre >= N".  NewMine uses 2.
#   - vp_occ_clear_cells (default 2): Chebyshev occupied-clearance radius;
#     0 disables the ring check (8-neighbour exclusion still applies).
#     NewMine uses 0.
#   - go_home_ is cleared whenever getCentroid succeeds again.
# Launch: lrae_go2/launch/lrae_newmine.launch sets both params.

# ============================================================================
# Fix 3 (2026-11-04): frontier fallback + goal-distance floor + hysteresis.
#
# Run #2 (viewpoint relaxation only) stalled at (4.1, 1.6): viewpoints existed
# (49 candidates, 27 reachable) but route/path planning failed repeatedly
# ("Replan." x21) and go_home_ re-latched; the earlier unlatch was dead code
# (placed below the early return).
#
# exploration_planning.{h,cpp}:
#   - publishFrontierFallback(): BFS from the robot over traversable cells
#     (< 95) to the nearest/last-valid unknown-adjacent cell >= goal_min_dis_
#     away; publishes the cell path on /exporation_path.  Called whenever no
#     path was published this cycle (no centroid + empty outwin, outwin path
#     failure, Replan, go_home_ latch) — the latch branch now probes the
#     fallback instead of returning forever, so go_home_ recovers.
#   - publishExplorationPathFiltered(): drops published goals whose endpoint
#     is < goal_min_dis_ (default 1.2, NewMine launch 0.7 m) from the robot;
#     a nearer goal sits inside pathFollower's stopDisThre (0.2) + look-ahead
#     deadband, so the robot never reaches it, the map never updates and the
#     same goal repeats forever (run #3 dither).
#   - Goal hysteresis on the fallback target (last_fb_goal_) with
#     reachability re-check; without it the robot spins between competing
#     nearest-frontier goals (run #5/#6: 76 m walked, |wz|>0.3 on 71% of
#     cycles, coverage plateaus).
#
# Result (10-min NewMine runs): run #1 (upstream) froze at t=44 s, 6.4 m,
# coverage +50 m2 then flat; run #6 with fixes: no freeze, 75.6 m walked,
# tracking r=0.99 cmd->actual; remaining limitation: coverage still plateaus
# at ~3 min (limit cycle at the merge boundary), see results notes.
